# Pins Ruby method-name parity on String: `upcase`/`downcase` (aliases of
# `to_upper`/`to_lower`) and `length` (alias of `size`), sharing the same C
# symbols. The Ruxen spellings keep working alongside the Ruby ones.
def main
  let s = "Hello World"
  puts(s.upcase)
  puts(s.downcase)
  puts(s.to_upper)
  puts(s.to_lower)
  puts(s.length)
  puts(s.size)
end
